' ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════
' IFD-001: MC ↔ FCC  (uXRCE-DDS)
' ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════
== IFD-001 · MC ↔ FCC · uXRCE-DDS · ttyTHS1 921600 / 192.168.12.x UDP:8888 ==

FCC -[#E07000]> MC : <color:#E07000>vehicle_local_position</color>  ≥10 Hz\n  x,y,z (NED m)  ·  vx,vy,vz (m/s)  ·  heading (rad)  ·  xy_valid, z_valid
FCC -[#E07000]> MC : <color:#E07000>vehicle_global_position</color>  ≥5 Hz\n  lat,lon (degE7)  ·  alt_msl (m)  ·  eph,epv (m)
FCC -[#E07000]> MC : <color:#E07000>vehicle_status</color>  ≥5 Hz\n  nav_state  ·  arming_state  ·  failure_detector_status (bitmask)
FCC -[#E07000]> MC : <color:#E07000>battery_status</color>  ≥2 Hz\n  voltage_v  ·  current_a  ·  remaining (0–1)  ·  warning level
FCC -[#E07000]> MC : <color:#E07000>vehicle_attitude</color>  ≥50 Hz\n  q[4] quaternion [w,x,y,z] NED→body
FCC -[#E07000]> MC : <color:#E07000>vehicle_odometry</color>  ≥20 Hz\n  position[3]  ·  q[4]  ·  velocity[3]  ·  angular_velocity[3]
FCC -[#E07000]> MC : <color:#E07000>sensor_combined</color>  ≥100 Hz\n  gyro_rad[3] (rad/s)  ·  accelerometer_m_s2[3]

MC -[#E07000]> FCC : <color:#E07000>vehicle_command</color>  (event-driven)\n  ARM/DISARM (400)  ·  SET_MODE (176)  ·  TAKEOFF (22)  ·  RTL (20)  ·  HOLD (17)  ·  OFFBOARD (176/custom)
MC -[#E07000]> FCC : <color:#E07000>vehicle_visual_odometry</color>  ≥10 Hz  (GNSS-denied only)\n  position[3] NED  ·  q[4]  ·  velocity[3]  ·  position_variance[3]
MC -[#E07000]> FCC : <color:#E07000>offboard_control_mode</color> + <color:#E07000>trajectory_setpoint</color>  ≥5 Hz  (FCC-009)\n  position=true only  ·  x,y,z (NED m) · yaw (rad)  ·  velocity/accel/jerk NaN'd (uncontrolled)\n  only while active mission plan flags the current leg for OFFBOARD  [FR-020/026-029]

note over FCC, MC #FFF0E0
  FccBackend abstraction: application nodes use /mc/fcc/* topics only.
  Transport (serial / ethernet) is a deployment config — no code changes.
  Latency FCC actuation: ≤ 100 ms  [IR-006]
  stream_offboard_setpoint() sends no DO_SET_MODE — mode entry/exit stays
  vehicle_command, sole authority mission_manager_node  [FCC-009]
end note

== IFD-001b · MC ↔ FCC · Mission Protocol (MAVLink 2/UDP) · 192.168.12.31:14555 — always ethernet ==

note over FCC, MC #F5ECF5
  Stock PX4 has no DDS-writable mission topic — items live in FCC-side
  dataman, reachable only via the standard MAVLink mission protocol.
  This is the ONE MAVLink exception on the MC↔FCC link.  [IR-007]
  Independent of FCC_TRANSPORT (§ above) — always active on 192.168.12.x.
end note

MC -[#C020A0]> FCC : <color:#C020A0>MISSION_COUNT</color>  →  <color:#C020A0>MISSION_ITEM_INT</color> ×N  →  <color:#C020A0>MISSION_ACK</color>\n  full upload, on mission change only  ·  search paths, ingress/muster legs (FR-013)\n  item: seq · frame=GLOBAL_INT · command (NAV_WAYPOINT=16) · lat,lon (degE7) · alt_msl (m) · acceptance_radius (m)
MC -[#C020A0]> FCC : <color:#C020A0>MISSION_WRITE_PARTIAL_LIST</color>(seq,seq)  →  FCC <color:#C020A0>MISSION_REQUEST_INT</color>  →  <color:#C020A0>MISSION_ITEM_INT</color>  →  <color:#C020A0>MISSION_ACK</color>\n  single-item replace  ≥5 Hz (INGRESS)  ·  seq=0 = FORMATION_SLOT  (FR-020/FR-023)

note over FCC, MC #F5ECF5
  Handshake timeout: 500 ms with no MISSION_REQUEST_INT/MISSION_ACK
  → abort, retry on next control-loop tick (no blocking).
  MISSION mode only — no OFFBOARD.  MISSION mode has no PX4-imposed
  minimum update rate, so a gap does not cause a mode change.
end note

' ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════
' IFD-002: MC ↔ GCS  (MAVLink 2/UDP)
' ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════
== IFD-002 · MC ↔ GCS · MAVLink 2/UDP · recv :14552  send :14551  ·  sys_id=drone_id  comp_id=191 ==

GCS -[#208040]> MC : <color:#208040>HEARTBEAT (0)</color>  1 Hz\n  type=6 (GCS)  ·  autopilot=8
GCS -[#208040]> MC : <color:#208040>COMMAND_LONG (76)</color>  event\n  MC_CMD_PHASE_TRANSITION (50001)  param1 = phase_id\n  MC_CMD_ARM_AUTHORISE (50002)  param1 = mission_upload_id\n  MC_CMD_END_MISSION (50003)\n  MC_CMD_GCS_OVERRIDE (50004)  param1=1/0  param2=override_type
GCS -[#208040]> MC : <color:#208040>MISSION_COUNT (44)  →  MISSION_ITEM_INT (73) ×N  →  MISSION_ACK (47)</color>\n  Mission upload sequence  ·  mc_type=3\n  item cmds: 50200=ingress wpt  50201=muster  50202=formation offset\n             50203=search polygon vertex  50204=swarm peer entry

MC -[#208040]> GCS : <color:#208040>HEARTBEAT (0)</color>  1 Hz\n  type=18 (ONBOARD_CONTROLLER)  ·  system_status reflects phase
MC -[#208040]> GCS : <color:#208040>COMMAND_ACK (77)</color>  event  ≤500 ms\n  command echo  ·  result = MAV_RESULT  ·  on every GCS command
MC -[#208040]> GCS : <color:#208040>MC_STATUS (50100)</color>  ≥2 Hz\n  lat,lon (degE7)  ·  alt_msl (mm)  ·  heading (cdeg)  ·  groundspeed (cm/s)\n  battery_remaining (%)  ·  mission_phase  ·  localisation_mode\n  fault_mask (16-bit)  ·  peer_count  ·  isr_role
MC -[#208040]> GCS : <color:#208040>MC_DETECTION (50101)</color>  event  ≤1 s after detection\n  detection_id  ·  class_id + class_name[24]  ·  confidence (×10000)\n  lat,lon (degE7)  ·  alt_mm  ·  pos_uncertainty (cm)  ·  drone_id
MC -[#208040]> GCS : <color:#208040>MC_HEALTH (50103)</color>  ≥1 Hz\n  cpu_pct  ·  mem_pct  ·  disk_pct  ·  gpu_temp_c  ·  cpu_temp_c\n  fault_mask (16-bit)  ·  node_alive_mask (16-bit)  ·  uptime_s
MC -[#208040]> GCS : <color:#208040>STATUSTEXT (253)</color>  event\n  severity 0–7 (EMERGENCY → DEBUG)  ·  text[50]

note over MC, GCS #E8F4E8
  Channel B only — isolated from Channel A (GCS ↔ FCC, port 14550).
  All Channel B traffic routed via mavlink-router v4 in fcc-bridge container.
  GCS link-loss HOLD trigger: 10 s silence  [FR-073, SFR-007]
end note

' ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════
' IFD-003: MC ↔ Swarm Peers  (Swarm Protocol / UDP)
' ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════
== IFD-003 · MC ↔ Peers · Swarm Protocol/UDP · MANET 192.168.10.x · :14900 hb  :14901 coord ==

MC -[#7030A0]> PEERS : <color:#7030A0>SWARM_HEARTBEAT (0x01)</color>  1 Hz  →  all peers  ·  40 bytes\n  timestamp_us  ·  lat_e7, lon_e7, alt_mm  ·  vx,vy,vz\n  mission_phase  ·  battery_pct  ·  sensor_health  ·  fault_mask

PEERS -[#7030A0]> MC : <color:#7030A0>SWARM_HEARTBEAT (0x01)</color>  1 Hz  ←  each peer  ·  40 bytes\n  (same structure)  ·  LOST declared after 3 missed  [IR-023]

MC -[#7030A0]> PEERS : <color:#7030A0>ISR_CANDIDATE (0x10)</color>  event  (ISR_SELECTION phase)\n  battery_pct  ·  sensor_flags  ·  dist_to_centroid_m
PEERS -[#7030A0]> MC : <color:#7030A0>ISR_CANDIDATE (0x10)</color>  event  (from each peer)

MC -[#7030A0]> PEERS : <color:#7030A0>ISR_RESULT (0x11)</color>  event  (coordinator → all)\n  isr_count  ·  total_drones  ·  isr_ids[]
PEERS -[#7030A0]> MC : <color:#7030A0>ISR_RESULT_ACK (0x12)</color>  event  (each peer → coordinator)\n  accepted (1/0)

MC -[#7030A0]> PEERS : <color:#7030A0>VORONOI_PROPOSAL (0x20)</color>  event  (VORONOI_PARTITION phase)\n  round  ·  lat_e7, lon_e7, alt_m  (own position)
PEERS -[#7030A0]> MC : <color:#7030A0>VORONOI_PROPOSAL (0x20)</color>  event  (from each peer)

MC -[#7030A0]> PEERS : <color:#7030A0>VORONOI_ACCEPT (0x21)</color>  event  (after local computation)\n  round  ·  vertex_count  ·  vertices[] lat_e7,lon_e7  (CCW, own cell boundary)
PEERS -[#7030A0]> MC : <color:#7030A0>VORONOI_ACCEPT (0x21)</color>  event  (from each peer)

MC -[#7030A0]> PEERS : <color:#7030A0>PEER_STATE (0x30)</color>  ≥5 Hz  (INGRESS phase)  ·  52 bytes\n  x,y,z (NED m)  ·  vx,vy,vz  ·  heading  ·  q[4]  ·  is_leader

note over MC, PEERS #F0E8F8
  Header (12 bytes): protocol_version · sender_id · message_type · flags
                     sequence (uint16) · payload_length (uint16) · CRC-32
  Max tolerated latency: 500 ms  [IR-022]
  Peer LOST: 3 consecutive missed heartbeats (>3 s)  [IR-023]
end note

